#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:9
msgid "Mode matching a laser to a Fabry-Perot cavity"
msgstr "レーザーを Fabry-Perot 共振器にモードマッチングさせる"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:11
msgid ""
"A laser has to be coupled into a two-mirror Fabry-Perot cavity. The "
"cavity sits 3 m from the laser, and the two lenses between them are "
"picked from a stock of focal lengths."
msgstr ""
"レーザーを2枚鏡のファブリ・ペロー共振器に結合させる。共振器はレーザーから 3 m "
"のところにあり、間に置く2枚のレンズは、手持ちの焦点距離の中から選ぶ。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:14
msgid "Cavity"
msgstr "共振器"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:14
msgid "L = 1 m, ROC 2.5 m (input mirror) and 1.5 m (end mirror)"
msgstr "L = 1 m、曲率半径は 2.5 m（入力鏡）と 1.5 m（端鏡）"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:15
msgid "Laser"
msgstr "レーザー"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:15
msgid "waist diameter 0.2 mm, 3 m of path to the cavity"
msgstr "ウエスト直径 0.2 mm、共振器まで 3 m の光路"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:16
msgid "Free parameters"
msgstr "自由パラメータ"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:16
msgid "positions and focal lengths of the two lenses"
msgstr "2枚のレンズの位置と焦点距離"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:19
msgid ""
"The plan: find the eigenmode of the cavity first. Then build the real "
"bench in gtrace, where the lenses have a thickness and the input mirror "
"is a real substrate. The trace itself then says how good the coupling is."
msgstr ""
"手順はこうである。まず共振器の固有モードを求める。次に gtrace "
"で実際のベンチを組む。そこではレンズに厚みがあり、入射鏡は本物の基板である。結合の良し悪しは、トレース自身が教えてくれる。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:51
msgid "The eigenmode of the cavity"
msgstr "共振器の固有モード"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:53
msgid ""
"Two mirrors of radii :math:`R_1`, :math:`R_2` stand a distance :math:`L` "
"apart. Write :math:`g_i = 1 - L/R_i`. The cavity is stable when :math:`0 "
"< g_1 g_2 < 1`. The waist sits :math:`z_1 = "
"\\frac{g_2(1-g_1)}{g_1+g_2-2g_1g_2}L` from the input mirror, and the "
"Rayleigh range is :math:`z_R = "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{g_1g_2(1-g_1g_2)}{(g_1+g_2-2g_1g_2)^2}}\\,L`."
msgstr ""
"半径 :math:`R_1`\\ 、\\ :math:`R_2` の2枚のミラーが距離 :math:`L` を隔てて立っている。\\ "
":math:`g_i = 1 - L/R_i` と書く。共振器が安定なのは :math:`0 < g_1 g_2 < 1` "
"のときである。ウェストは入射鏡から :math:`z_1 = \\frac{g_2(1-g_1)}{g_1+g_2-2g_1g_2}L` "
"の位置にあり、レイリー長は :math:`z_R = "
"\\sqrt{\\frac{g_1g_2(1-g_1g_2)}{(g_1+g_2-2g_1g_2)^2}}\\,L` である。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:123
msgid "Confirming the eigenmode by ray tracing"
msgstr "固有モードを光線追跡で確認する"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:125
msgid ""
"The formulas above are the textbook eigenmode of a two-mirror cavity. "
"gtrace can produce the same answer from a ray trace."
msgstr "上の式は、教科書に載っている2枚鏡共振器の固有モードである。gtrace は同じ答えを光線追跡から出せる。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:127
msgid ""
"A ``GaussianBeam`` object carries two attributes, ``Mx`` and ``My``. They"
" hold the ABCD transformations the beam has received while propagating, "
"multiplied together. On a new beam they are the identity matrix."
msgstr ""
"``GaussianBeam`` オブジェクトは ``Mx`` と ``My`` の2つの属性を持つ。伝搬の間にビームが受けた ABCD "
"変換を、掛け合わせた形で保持している。新しく作ったビームでは単位行列である。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:129
msgid ""
"So send such a beam once around the cavity, and its ``Mx`` is the round-"
"trip ABCD matrix. Put a fresh beam on the surface of the ITM, propagate "
"it to the ETM and reflect it there, then reflect the returning beam at "
"the ITM. Read ``Mx`` and ``My`` off the beam object right after that "
"second reflection. In a system without astigmatism the two must agree."
msgstr ""
"だから、そのようなビームを共振器の中で1周させれば、その ``Mx`` が1周分の ABCD 行列になる。ITM の面に新しいビームを置き、ETM"
" まで伝搬させてそこで反射させ、戻ってきたビームを ITM で反射させる。2回目の反射の直後に、ビームオブジェクトから ``Mx`` と "
"``My`` を読む。非点収差の無い系では、この2つは一致するはずである。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:131
msgid "Write the matrix elements as"
msgstr "行列の要素を次のように書く"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:133
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A & B \\\\\n"
"C & D\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A & B \\\\\n"
"C & D\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:141
msgid "The eigenmode is the mode that returns to itself after one round trip, so"
msgstr "固有モードとは、1周して自分自身に戻るモードである。したがって"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:143
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"q = \\frac{Aq + B}{Cq + D}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"q = \\frac{Aq + B}{Cq + D}\n"
"\n"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:145
msgid ""
"has to be solved for :math:`q`. That is the quadratic :math:`Cq^2 + "
"(D-A)q - B = 0`, which has two roots. Take the root whose imaginary part "
"is positive, because the imaginary part is the Rayleigh range."
msgstr ""
"を :math:`q` について解けばよい。これは2次方程式 :math:`Cq^2 + (D-A)q - B = 0` "
"であり、根は2つある。虚部が正のほうの根を取る。虚部がレイリー長だからである。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:147
msgid ""
"When ``Mx`` and ``My`` differ, the eigenmode has a different q in the x "
"and the y direction."
msgstr "``Mx`` と ``My`` が違う場合、固有モードは x 方向と y 方向で違う q を持つ。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:251
msgid ""
"This way of getting the eigenmode out of a ray trace is general. It works"
" for three-mirror and bow-tie cavities as well."
msgstr "光線追跡から固有モードを取り出すこのやり方は一般的である。3枚鏡の共振器やボウタイ共振器でも同じように使える。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:263
msgid "The optical bench"
msgstr "光学ベンチ"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:265
msgid ""
"The cavity sits 3 m from the laser, with the two lenses in between. Call "
"the distance from the laser to the first lens (L1) d1, and the distance "
"from L1 to the second lens (L2) d2."
msgstr ""
"共振器はレーザーから 3 m のところにあり、間に2枚のレンズが入る。レーザーから1枚目のレンズ (L1) までの距離を d1、L1 "
"から2枚目のレンズ (L2) までの距離を d2 と呼ぶ。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:267
msgid "Laser -d1-> L1 -d2-> L2 -> ITM - ETM"
msgstr "Laser -d1-> L1 -d2-> L2 -> ITM - ETM"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:355
msgid "Moving the lenses: a contour map of the mode matching"
msgstr "レンズを動かす: モードマッチングの等高線図"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:357
msgid ""
"Once you choose a pair of focal lengths (f1, f2), the freedom left is the"
" two lens positions: d1 from the laser to L1, and d2 from L1 to L2. This "
"section does four things:"
msgstr ""
"焦点距離の組 (f1, f2) を選ぶと、残る自由度はレンズ2枚の位置である。レーザーから L1 までの d1 と、L1 から L2 までの d2"
" である。この節では4つのことを行う:"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:359
msgid ""
"Scan d1 and d2 on a 0.05 m grid, under the constraint d1 + d2 < 3.0, so "
"that L2 stays short of the ITM"
msgstr ""
"d1 + d2 < 3.0 という制約のもとで、d1 と d2 を 0.05 m 刻みの格子で走査する。L2 が ITM "
"の手前に留まるようにするためである"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:360
msgid ""
"At each grid point, place the lenses, run ``layout.trace()``, and pick "
"out the beam transmitted through the ITM, ``ITM:t1``"
msgstr "各格子点でレンズを配置し、\\ ``layout.trace()`` を実行し、ITM を透過したビーム ``ITM:t1`` を取り出す"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:361
msgid ""
"Compare the qx of that beam with the cavity eigenmode ``q_rt`` from the "
"previous section, using ``gauss.modeMatching()``. ``ITM:t1`` starts on "
"the HR surface of the ITM, and ``q_rt`` lives on the same surface, so the"
" two can be compared directly. 1 is a perfect match"
msgstr ""
"そのビームの qx を、前節で求めた共振器の固有モード ``q_rt`` と ``gauss.modeMatching()`` で比較する。\\ "
"``ITM:t1`` は ITM の HR 面から始まり、\\ ``q_rt`` も同じ面の上にあるので、そのまま比べられる。1 が完全一致である"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:362
msgid "Draw the result as a contour map over the d1-d2 plane"
msgstr "結果を d1-d2 平面上の等高線図として描く"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:364
msgid ""
"How to use this: put focal lengths from your stock into f1 and f2 at the "
"top of the cell and run it again. Look for a pair that produces a bright "
"region, which means a placement with high matching. The map gives you a "
"starting point, and a later section pins that candidate down by "
"optimisation."
msgstr ""
"使い方はこうである。セルの先頭の f1 と f2 "
"に手持ちの焦点距離を入れて、もう一度実行する。明るい領域ができる組を探す。それがマッチングの高い配置である。この図は出発点を与える。あとの節で、その候補を最適化によって詰める。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:475
msgid "Speeding it up: running the scan in parallel"
msgstr "高速化: 走査を並列で走らせる"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:477
msgid ""
"The scan above calls ``layout.trace()`` once per grid point. On the 0.05 "
"m grid that is about 1600 points and takes some ten seconds. If you "
"redraw the map many times while trying different lenses, joblib can "
"spread the work over every CPU core. On a 20-core machine this took the "
"scan from 10.6 s to 1.7 s, and the results were identical to the serial "
"scan."
msgstr ""
"上の走査は、格子点ごとに ``layout.trace()`` を1回呼ぶ。0.05 m "
"刻みの格子ではおよそ1600点あり、10秒ほどかかる。レンズを変えながら図を何度も描き直すなら、joblib で全ての CPU "
"コアに仕事を分けられる。20コアのマシンでは、この走査が 10.6 秒から 1.7 秒になり、結果は逐次版と完全に一致した。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:479
msgid "Three points about the code below:"
msgstr "下のコードについて3点:"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:481
msgid ""
"In a notebook on Windows, the standard ``multiprocessing`` cannot send "
"functions defined in the notebook to its workers. **joblib** (the loky "
"backend) sends the function itself, so you can write the code the way it "
"reads"
msgstr ""
"Windows の notebook では、標準の ``multiprocessing`` は notebook "
"の中で定義した関数をワーカーへ送れない。\\ **joblib**\\ （loky "
"バックエンド）は関数そのものを送るので、読んだとおりのコードを書ける"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:482
msgid ""
"Each worker builds **its own private bench** in ``build_bench()``, so no "
"objects are shared between processes. The scan therefore never touches "
"the ``layout`` of this notebook or its viewer"
msgstr ""
"各ワーカーは ``build_bench()`` で\\ **自分専用のベンチ**\\ "
"を組む。だからプロセス間でオブジェクトを共有しない。走査がこの notebook の ``layout`` やそのビューアに触ることは無い"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:483
msgid ""
"The unit of parallel work is **one column of the map** (``scan_row``), "
"not one point. Handed out point by point, the cost of moving data between"
" the processes would be larger than the computation"
msgstr ""
"並列の作業単位は1点ではなく、\\ **図の1列**\\ （\\ ``scan_row``\\ "
"）である。1点ずつ配ると、プロセス間でデータを運ぶ費用のほうが計算より大きくなる"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:485
msgid ""
"The worker processes take a few seconds to start the first time, and "
"later runs of the cell reuse them. The second scan and the ones after it "
"are therefore the fastest."
msgstr "ワーカープロセスは、最初の1回だけ起動に数秒かかり、以降のセル実行では再利用される。だから2回目以降の走査がいちばん速い。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:620
msgid "Pinning down d1 and d2 by optimisation"
msgstr "最適化で d1 と d2 を詰める"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:622
msgid ""
"The contour map uses a 0.05 m grid, which is enough to find a starting "
"point. From here an optimiser takes over. Start from the ``d1_init``, "
"``d2_init`` you read off the map, and minimise 1 - matching with "
"``scipy.optimize.minimize`` (Nelder-Mead)."
msgstr ""
"等高線図は 0.05 m 刻みで、出発点を見つけるには十分である。ここから先は最適化に任せる。図から読み取った ``d1_init``\\ 、\\"
" ``d2_init`` を初期値として、1 - matching を ``scipy.optimize.minimize``\\ "
"（Nelder-Mead）で最小化する。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:624
msgid ""
"The cost function reuses ``matching()`` from above. One trace takes a few"
" milliseconds and the optimisation needs about a hundred evaluations, so "
"it does not need to run in parallel"
msgstr ""
"コスト関数は上の ``matching()`` "
"をそのまま使う。1回のトレースは数ミリ秒で、最適化に必要な評価は百回程度なので、並列で走らせる必要は無い"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:625
msgid ""
"Nelder-Mead uses no derivatives. That suits a cost which comes out of a "
"trace and has no formula for its gradient"
msgstr "Nelder-Mead は微分を使わない。トレースから出てくる、勾配の式が無いコストに向いている"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:626
msgid ""
"The constraints (positive lens separations, L2 short of the ITM) are a "
"penalty: outside them the cost is the worst value, 1. **If the optimum "
"comes back sitting on a constraint boundary**, this pair of lenses has no"
" true optimum inside the constraints. Try a different pair of focal "
"lengths"
msgstr ""
"制約（レンズ間隔が正であること、L2 が ITM の手前にあること）はペナルティで表す。制約の外ではコストを最悪値の 1 にする。\\ "
"**最適解が制約の境界に張り付いて返ってきた場合**\\ 、そのレンズの組には制約の内側に真の最適解が無い。別の焦点距離の組を試すこと"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:628
msgid ""
"An example: with f1 = 500 mm and f2 = -500 mm the map is bright around d1"
" = 1.4, d2 = 0.4. Started there, 64 traces reach matching = 1.000000, so "
"this pair can be matched perfectly by positioning alone."
msgstr ""
"例を挙げる。f1 = 500 mm、f2 = -500 mm では、図は d1 = 1.4、d2 = 0.4 "
"のあたりが明るい。そこから始めると、64回のトレースで matching = 1.000000 "
"に達する。この組は、配置だけで完全にマッチングできる。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:710
msgid "Checking the result in the viewer"
msgstr "結果をビューアで確認する"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:712
msgid ""
"Click a beam near the ITM surface and confirm that its ROC is close to "
"2.5 m, the ROC of the ITM. Do the same on the ETM: the ROC of the mirror "
"and the ROC of the beam agree there too."
msgstr ""
"ITM の面の近くでビームをクリックし、その ROC が ITM の ROC である 2.5 m に近いことを確かめる。ETM "
"でも同じことをする。そちらでも、ミラーの ROC とビームの ROC が一致している。"

#: ../../../gtrace/docs/source/tutorial/modematching.ipynb:714
msgid ""
"A beam that ends on a surface sits under the element itself. Click the "
"same spot again to step from the element to the beams under it."
msgstr "面で終わるビームは、素子そのものの下にある。同じ場所をもう一度クリックすると、素子からその下のビームへ進む。"

#~ msgid "Three points:"
#~ msgstr "3点だけ注意がある:"

